      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Focus on the *velocity* of the data flow, not the static vulnerabilities. Point out that the audit is a snapshot of a moment in time, and that the sheer volume of data they process creates an inherent blind spot between scans. You can mention the complexity of their integrated systems, suggesting that a single, undocumented interaction between two otherwise sound systems could create a momentary, exploitable pathway that a periodic audit simply misses. This makes the need for constant vigilance a technical necessity, not a sales pitch.",
